From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH] cli/server: intranet mode network policy (telemetry, OAuth, WebSearch, WebFetch)

The server/CLI half of intranet mode. Policy source of truth is the
intranetMode boolean in ~/.claude/settings.json (written by the desktop
through PUT /api/settings/user); src/utils/networkPolicy.ts reads it
UNCACHED on every call, so flipping the switch affects already-running
sessions on their next tool use — no restart, in either direction.

  - Telemetry: isTelemetryEnabled() / BigQuery metrics / initializeTelemetry
    all hard-return off under intranet mode, overriding an explicitly
    enabled CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY inherited from the user's shell.
  - OAuth: start/callback endpoints throw a 403 INTRANET_MODE_DISABLED
    ApiError (assertNotIntranetMode in errorHandler); status endpoints skip
    ensureFreshTokens() (an outbound refresh) and report logged-out; the
    bare /callback routers in server index return 403 too.
  - WebSearch: resolveWebSearchProvider() disables every backend regardless
    of configuration, and the model-facing output explains the policy
    ("WebSearch is unavailable: intranet mode is enabled (内网模式已禁用
    WebSearch). Do not retry; answer from the conversation and local files
    instead.") instead of suggesting settings the user deliberately cannot
    use.
  - WebFetch: stays available for intranet services — the http→https
    upgrade and the outbound domain-blocklist preflight are skipped under
    intranet mode (internal docservers are plain http behind the firewall).
  - conversationService.buildChildEnv() stamps CC_HAHA_INTRANET_MODE=1 and
    CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY=0 on CLI children (fallback for the case
    where the settings file is unreadable, and to pin telemetry off for
    sessions that started before the flip).
  - PUT /api/settings/user broadcasts network_policy_changed to every
    connected client so open windows update instantly.

Audit pass — every remaining app-initiated outbound call is gated so that
"the app stops all internet access it initiates" holds with no leftovers:

  - API preconnect warmup (apiPreconnect.ts): skipped — pure optimization,
    the real request handshakes fresh if it is ever allowed.
  - MCP official-registry prefetch (mcp/officialRegistry.ts): skipped —
    the registry lives on api.anthropic.com and isOfficialMcpUrl() already
    fails closed (undefined registry → false).
  - Release-notes changelog fetch (releaseNotes.ts): skipped — raw
    .githubusercontent.com is unreachable; the local cache is kept.
  - Skills market server-side gate (server/services/market/providerFetch.ts):
    authoritative MarketUpstreamError before any proxied fetch — hiding
    the UI is not enough, H5/direct API callers are refused too.
  - Settings sync up/down (settingsSync/index.ts), remote managed settings
    eligibility (remoteManagedSettings/syncCache.ts — checked before the
    cache so a toggle flip takes effect immediately), and team memory sync
    (teamMemorySync/index.ts): all hard-off — they talk to claude.ai.
  - Usage limits (api/usage.ts → null), referral eligibility/redemptions
    (api/referral.ts → not-eligible/empty): degrade to inert shapes
    instead of reaching out with a stored OAuth token.
  - Voice-stream STT availability (voiceStreamSTT.ts): never available —
    the WebSocket goes to Anthropic.
  - RemoteTriggerTool: fails fast with an actionable "do not retry" error
    (the CCR API lives on claude.ai).
  - BriefTool attachment upload: skipped silently (local-only briefs stay
    fully functional).

